# PART 3 — COMPLETE AUDIO PLAYER FIX AND IMPROVEMENTS

Inspect the existing Audio Player and fix all playback-related bugs.

### Existing Bugs to Fix

- Audio plays but the Player displays an incorrect Pause or Play icon.
- Pause does not correctly stop playback.
- Clicking Play after Pause restarts Audio from the beginning.
- Playback Position is not saved correctly.
- Progress Bar does not match the actual Audio Position.
- Multiple Audio Instances play simultaneously.
- Chapter changes cause incorrect playback state.
- Auto Next does not work correctly.

### Required Audio Controls

Implement or fix:

1. Play.
2. Pause.
3. Resume from the exact paused position.
4. Previous Chapter.
5. Next Chapter.
6. Progress Bar.
7. Seek Forward by 10 seconds.
8. Seek Backward by 10 seconds.
9. Playback Speed.
10. Volume Control.
11. Mute and Unmute.
12. Sleep Timer.
13. Auto Next Chapter.
14. Background Playback.
15. Lock Screen Controls where supported.

### Playback Speeds

Provide:

- 0.5x
- 0.75x
- 1x
- 1.25x
- 1.5x
- 2x

### Technical Requirements

- The actual HTMLAudioElement state must be the source of truth.
- Properly handle play, pause, ended, waiting, error and timeupdate events.
- Update UI from actual playback events.
- Prevent duplicate Audio Instances.
- Properly clean up event listeners.
- Save playback position for each User, Novel and Chapter.
- Restore playback position when returning.
- Preserve position after Browser Refresh.
- Chapter changes must reset the old Audio correctly.
- Do not reset Audio Position when switching between Text and Audio Mode.

### Previous and Next Chapter

Previous and Next Chapter controls must be clearly available in the Audio Player.

Previous Chapter:
- Start the previous available Chapter.
- Disable the button if no previous Chapter exists.
- Restore the previous Chapter's saved Audio Position if available.

Next Chapter:
- Start the next authorized Chapter.
- Disable the button if no next Chapter exists.
- Restore its saved Audio Position if available.

When switching Chapters, the old Audio must stop completely before the new Audio starts.

The current Chapter Title and Chapter Number must be visible.

Audio Navigation must synchronize with Text Reading Navigation.

Do not bypass Free and Premium Chapter Permissions.

### TTS Requirements

If a Chapter uses Text-to-Speech:

- Handle Speech Synthesis separately from normal Audio Files.
- Do not pretend unsupported TTS seeking is available.
- Save progress using the best supported method.
- Display the actual TTS playback state.
- Do not break normal Audio File Playback.

